  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n(4, 8, 256)\n\n(2, 9, 144)\n\n**Logic: **Third no. = [(First no.) × (Second no.) × 8]\n\n(4, 8, 256) →\n\n⇒ [(4) × (8) × (8)]\n\n⇒ (32 × 8) = 256\n\n(2, 9, 144) →\n\n⇒ [(2) × (9) × (8)]\n\n⇒ (18 × 8) = 144\n\nChecking all the given options:\n\n**1. (6, 9, 432) **→\n\n⇒ [(6) × (9) × (8)]\n\n⇒ (54 × 8) = **432**\n\n**2. (4, 9, 258) **→\n\n⇒ [(4) × (9) × (8)]\n\n⇒ (36 × 8) = 288\n\n**3. (8, 5, 340) **→\n\n⇒ [(8) × (5) × (8)]\n\n⇒ (40 × 8) = 320\n\n**4. (3, 7, 162) **→\n\n⇒ [(3) × (7) × (8)]\n\n⇒ (21 × 8) = 168\n\nHere, (6, 9, 432) shows a similar relation to the given set of numbers.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option (1)\".",
